# Skyclave Apparition's "nonland, nontoken permanent you don't control with mana value 4 or less": Bot2 dashes a Ragavan on turn 2
# (it connects: a Treasure token), plays an Island and keeps a Mox Ruby and a Mox Jet. On turn 3 the Apparition's trigger cannot
# target the Treasure (a token), the Island (a land) or Bot1's own Mox Pearl (not "you don't control"), but can target the
# Mox Jet, which is exiled (the positive control). The Treasure Token and the Island stay.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Skyclave Apparition
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer
Island
Plains x4
Plains x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer.Cast(Ability: Dash)
Bot2.Attack(Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer > Bot1)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#3.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Skyclave Apparition.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Treasure Token)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 2
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Mox Ruby; Treasure Token
